* metadata_report_regression.dts -- METAREPORT
*
* THE REPORTS THAT NAME A CONTAINER, AN ENV OR AN ORDER MUST NAME THE ONE THE
* ENGINE ACTUALLY USES (2026-09-10, from the metadata scan of the same day).
*
* EVERY CLAIM IN THIS FILE IS CONSOLE TEXT AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS A MARKER.
* A marker in this language is a FIELD-VALUE comparison, so it cannot read a
* path, an envdir or a parenthetical -- the limit already recorded against
* LIST, COUNT and RECNO (the IDXDIFF precedent). The instrument here is
* MetadataReportV1 in cmd_regression.cpp, which reads the ROUTED CAPTURE and
* grades eight fenced blocks. If a block is MISSING the validator says so and
* fails: a lost claim is not a pass, which is the COUNT THE MARKERS rule
* applied to fences instead of verdicts.
*
* NOTHING IS COMPARED AGAINST A LITERAL PATH, ON PURPOSE. Absolute paths are
* machine-specific and this tree already carries that debt elsewhere. Every
* path assertion here is RELATIONAL: a value read from one verb must equal a
* value read from another verb, or must carry a given extension. A clone with
* a different drive letter grades identically.
*
* READ-ONLY. Opens shipped fixtures, creates nothing, erases nothing, mints no
* catalog row (none of the three minting verbs appear). It re-points the DBF,
* INDEXES and LMDB slots and the harness restores them.
*
* WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, stated rather than implied:
*   - That CDX INFO's per-tag counts are right. They are not asserted; see the
*     open question recorded 2026-09-10 -- every tag prints root_off=0 recs=0
*     over a 200-row table while the CNX reader prints entries=200 for the same
*     six names. That is a separate finding and a separate fix.
*   - Anything about a SECOND workspace. The discriminator here is a SLOT THAT
*     MOVES, which is strictly cheaper and reaches the same defect.
*   - That these arms have ever gone RED. They have not been run against a
*     pre-fix binary; the predictions are in the registry entry.

*
* PATHS ARE RELATIVE TO THE DATA ROOT, like every other spec in this tree.
* An absolute path in a TRACKED spec is the debt the PKDURABLE child scripts
* already carry and it is recorded there as a debt, not as a pattern. If a
* relative token ever failed to resolve, the fixture would not open and the
* validator would report the EMPTY BLOCK explicitly -- "the verb inside it
* printed nothing" -- which is a different finding from a wrong answer and is
* reported as one.

SET ECHO OFF
SET STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

? "METAREPORT-BEGIN"

WORKSPACE CLOSE

SET PATH DBF DBF\x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES\x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB\x64

USE STUDENTS
SET ORDER TAG SID

* ---- P1 CONTROL. The slot still agrees with the attachment, so BOTH a fixed
* ---- and a broken build answer the same thing here. Its only job is to hand
* ---- P2 a reference value. Graded as a control, never as evidence.
? "MR-P1-BEGIN"
CDX INFO
? "MR-P1-END"

* ---- P2 MEASUREMENT. The INDEXES slot now points somewhere the container is
* ---- NOT. A build whose reuse branch fires answers from the ATTACHMENT and
* ---- still names P1's container; a build that falls through to
* ---- resolve_cdx_token(stem) answers from the SLOT and names SANDBOX.
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES\SANDBOX
? "MR-P2-BEGIN"
CDX INFO
? "MR-P2-END"

* ---- P3 THE MIRROR, and the half that actually bit. With a .CNX attached the
* ---- old predicate FIRED and handed the .cnx path back to a CDX verb, which
* ---- then reported not-found on a file that exists. READ THE EXTENSION, NOT
* ---- THE VERDICT: not-found is the correct answer here because the x32 tree
* ---- has no .cdx. What is graded is that the path ends .cdx and that no .cnx
* ---- appears in the block at all.
SET PATH DBF DBF\x32
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES\x32
WORKSPACE CLOSE
USE STUDENTS
SET CNX STUDENTS.cnx
? "MR-P3-BEGIN"
CDX INFO
? "MR-P3-END"

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF\x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES\x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB\x64
USE STUDENTS

* ---- P4 THE ORACLE, from a verb nobody changed. SET INDEX prints the env the
* ---- backend opens. This is what makes P5 assertable without a literal path.
? "MR-P4-BEGIN"
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS.cdx
? "MR-P4-END"

* ---- P5 MEASUREMENT. The echoed envdir must EQUAL P4's. The old form glued
* ---- ".d" onto the container path, which lands under INDEXES; the backend
* ---- opens what resolve_lmdb_env_for_cdx returns, rooted at LMDB. The two
* ---- slots are deliberately different roots in this run.
? "MR-P5-BEGIN"
SET LMDB STUDENTS SID
? "MR-P5-END"

WORKSPACE CLOSE
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS.cdx

* ---- P6 AIF-148 on SET LMDB. A container is attached and NO tag is chosen,
* ---- which is the state WORKSPACE OPEN leaves behind. The line used to say
* ---- TAG '' (ASC) -- an empty tag beside a direction, refuting itself in one
* ---- breath.
? "MR-P6-BEGIN"
SET LMDB
? "MR-P6-END"

* ---- P7 the same shape on the verb NAMED SET ORDER, which was the last one
* ---- still wrong after order_report, index_summary and status_helpers were
* ---- repaired for exactly this.
? "MR-P7-BEGIN"
SET ORDER
? "MR-P7-END"

* ---- P8 THE COUNTERWEIGHT, and the reason the fix cannot overshoot. A change
* ---- that forced PHYSICAL unconditionally would pass P6 and P7 and be exactly
* ---- as wrong as the defect. Choose a tag and a real direction must come back.
SET ORDER TAG LNAME
? "MR-P8-BEGIN"
SET ORDER
? "MR-P8-END"

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF\x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES\x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB\x64

? "METAREPORT-END"
